U.S. Reports volumes 300–399 — Caselaw Access Project
Collection ID: caselaw-us-300-399
Package coverage: caselaw-us-300-399-part-NNNN archives share these content licenses.
Source: https://static.case.law/
Collection definition: https://github.com/bendyline/knowledge/blob/main/collections/caselaw/us-300-399/collection.json
License: CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0-1.0)
Terms: https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
Full license text and source evidence: included in every archive's LICENSES directory.
Attribution: Caselaw Access Project, Harvard Law School Library; credit is voluntary under CAP community norms.
Scope: Every CAP case record in U.S. Reports volumes 300–399, preserving source jurisdiction, court labels, and decision dates, including four source dates earlier than the books' 1937–1970 period. This bounded historical reporter collection contains the earlier 347–349 pilot in full; installing both duplicates those records. It is not the complete U.S. Reports or federal collection.

